---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Security and trust | Prodory" description="How Prodory handles access, data and changes, and what we can share on request." path="/security/">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-14">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm text-muted"><a href="/">Home</a> / Security</nav>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Security and trust</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted">This page describes how we work. It makes no certification claims: we will share evidence for any statement on request.</p>

    <section class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Access</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Named accounts only, no shared logins. We start from read-only access and widen it per change, with approval.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Changes</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Production changes go through reviewed pull requests, with a logged rollback plan.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Data</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Encryption in transit and at rest is designed into every platform we build. Data residency follows your rules, not ours.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold">Logging</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Audit logs are retained per your obligations, with the retention period set in the design (DPDP and CERT-In are the usual references in India).</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 rounded-xl bg-card p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Security pack on request</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">Read-only IAM policy examples, the encryption and logging posture for a typical engagement, and our breach-handling procedure. Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">Grievance contact under the DPDP Act: to be named before 13 May 2027. Until then, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
